format session-log-v1
stamp 20260823.041442
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Nothing was lost
prompt Keaton approved the recommendations and said kg -- take the two agent-doable items: unify expanded-prompts into expanding-prompts with a cairn, and build the empty-document guard closing REDS %161.
think Read the approval narrowly on one point. `%162` names three resolutions -- make the field private, restore signing, debride the personal material -- and my recommendation there was that Keaton pick among them, not that I act. Two touch published history, so the gate stays open and untouched.
think Took the unify as a genuine breach: cairn first, then the cut. Recorded the walk-back nib 997ba249af in crux/CAIRNS.md BEFORE moving anything, per the cairn rule.
think Found the real reason the unify is right rather than merely cheap. The two rooms were seated 20260810 to file intent by temperature, and the date/YYYYMMDD/ fold seated AFTER them already carries that distinction structurally -- flat at the room root is hot, folded under date/ is cold. The second room had become a second way of saying one thing.
think Swept inbound references three ways -- relative path, bare name, slug -- and split them by tier. Machinery repointed (banner_room_scan.sh, template-manifest.bron, .gitignore); the three seating rows in LEXICON, TASKS, and REMEMBER amended to name the unify beside the elder reading; dated testimony and the session-log index rows describing that day left exactly as written.
think On %161 I checked git before writing anything, because the honest root matters more than a tidy repair. Both files were BORN at zero bytes in 758d64e639 and never corrupted -- git ls-tree -l reads size 0 at their own seating commit.
think Then found the records were never lost at all: both laps wrote themselves into the waymark room, e121 at 1,759 bytes and e122 beside its counsel. So the repair is a pointer rather than an epitaph, and I rewrote the two rows I had drafted claiming the content was unrecoverable.
think Filling beat removing. The session log is indexed in session-logs/README.md and the empty prompt is cited by name in two later prompts; deleting either would break references to fix a blank. Filling is pure accretion -- there was no content to preserve -- and every citation now resolves to something true.
obs The guard's first shape spawned one `git cat-file` per document and took 33 seconds over 8,486 files. One `--batch-check` over all shas, filtered to those under 64 bytes before reading any, brings it to 0.16s with every field identical. Two shapes agreeing on 8,486 is worth more than one shape reading confidently.
obs Broke the fixture exemption once while speeding it up -- a shell regex with a stray escape stopped excluding tools/fixtures/ and the scan reddened on its own controls. Moved the whole filter into one awk so no shell-regex escaping stands between the rule and the reading.
obs Named the fixture exemption as a rule rather than remembering it. That lesson has now fired three times -- %157 a planted basename quoted in a log, %158 a control planting what its own guard refuses, %161 a scan reddening on four fixture files -- and a lantern that fires twice becomes a loom.
obs The rung counts presence, never quality: one character passes. The fix for a thin document is a reader, not a byte count, and a guard that tried to measure worth would be guessing.
obs REDS crossed its bound again; row %160 folded to crux/archive/ with a doorway line. Its open remainder -- 848 seed-dead links -- needs no row to stay visible, because seed_link reports the count on every run.
loom witness=empty_document scan_wall_ms=163 prior_shape_wall_ms=32758 tracked_documents=8486 empty=0 control_behaviors=14
loom unify=expanded_prompts files_moved=1 files_removed=1 living_refs_repointed=3 seating_rows_amended=3 cairn=997ba249af
file tools/fixtures/empty_document_scan.sh gates tracked documents at zero, fixtures free as instrument, one batch-check pass
file tools/fixtures/empty_document_control.sh fourteen behaviors on real repositories -- five refusals bitten, nine readings left free
file tools/empty_document_witness.rish the rung, and what it deliberately does not measure
file session-logs/date/20260731/20260731-220432_e121-roots-bench-amend-green.bron filled with a pointer to the waymark that holds the record
file expanding-prompts/archive/20260731-220432_equinox-season-e122-recursion-prompt.md filled with pointers to the waymark and counsel
file expanding-prompts/date/20260810/20260810-054332_green-witness-record-seed-ready.md the one record carried over from the retired room
file crux/CAIRNS.md the walk-back recorded before the cut, with what waits there worth recalling
file context/LEXICON.md the two-temperature term amended to one room and a fold
file crux/REDS.md %161 closed, the unify recorded as not-a-red, row %160 folded under bound
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- %162 is still the open gate and still yours: all three remotes read PUBLIC, so the seed's unsigned commit protects a field that already publishes a resume, a personal ontology, a cover letter, and the poems. Everything else is green and the loops are ready. If you want the outer loop restarted before that ruling, say so plainly and I will note the gate stays open while it runs.
